Error [E0224]: This call writes `solver`, but `solver` has no `&` mark
  --> builtin_mut_receiver_uses_two_phase_reservation_5.jet:5:5
    |
  5 |     solver.require(solver.failure_count() == 0)
    |     ^^^^^^
 Why: The method is declared with `&self`, so the call writes the named place it is called on; the mark sits on that place, the same way `edit(&buf)` and `consume(^text)` mark arguments
 Fix: Write `&solver`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0224
